{"agent_id":"pp3g-jHj4-review-r1-hy3-primary-154-durable-fork-implementation","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:55:01.854527055Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"83be1dc0-30d2-48de-9dd6-0bd560241e3f","comment_uuid":"4aae9cd2-9766-4d8a-97ee-5b9cf76eb55c","author":"pp3g-jHj4-review-r1-hy3-primary-154-durable-fork-implementation","content":"=== RESULT PART 1/3 — VERDICT: PASS ===\nThe #154 durable source fix (commit 98dfe4a) is CORRECT and COMPILE-READY. The row-1 4-POST-vs-3 discrepancy is a HARNESS/TEST-ISOLATION artifact, NOT a product defect in the 3-POST bound.\n\n--- (1) safeIterable() correctness — PASS ---\nFile: llm.ts:43-60 (fork-build packages/opencode/src/session/llm.ts:43-60).\nRoot cause of #154: effect Stream.fromAsyncIterable installs a scope finalizer that AWAITS the iterator return(). After a provider stream error (wrapBodyIdle/wrapSSE idle timeout), the ai@6 fullStream return() can reject/hang, deadlocking runDrain into the silent hang.\nFix: safeIterable wraps the iterator so return() fires iter.return?.() in the background (void Promise.resolve(...).catch(()=>{})) and immediately resolves {done:true}. The error already propagated via next() rejection before return() is invoked, so no error masking; cleanup becomes best-effort + non-blocking.\nCorrectness: next delegates; return() try/catch guards a synchronous throw from iter.return?.(), a rejecting promise is swallowed by .catch, always returns {done:true}. No deadlock path remains. No stubs/TODOs.\nWHY: removes the only mechanism by which a body-idle error converts into an infinite hang.\nWHAT: based on llm.ts + provider.ts wrapBodyIdle (provider.ts:89-144) which errors the stream on idle.\nHOW-CERTAIN: evidence-based (high) — logic self-consistent with the #154 signature; runtime confirmation is the #235 gate (row1 fires 'Body read timed out' + exit 1).\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: did not execute the binary; rests on source reasoning + #235 gate.\n\n--- (2) Compile-readiness — PASS ---\n- 'Body read timed out' present: provider.ts:122 (ProviderError.ResponseStreamError). OK\n- 'Turn stalled' present: llm.ts:433 (Stream.timeoutOrElse orElse). OK\n- ERROR-level surfacing + exit 1 (not 124): error propagates Stream.fail -> Effect.retry(SessionRetry.policy) -> processor Effect.catch(halt) -> Session.Event.Error + process exit 1; safeIterable guarantees no hang-to-124. OK\n- 3-POST budget: see Part 2.","created_at":"2026-08-08T04:55:01.846816272Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:FXJFKYYquT8mBMevltVEZAczkbT+oJL1T6Eb6+jrkBc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNg9sGUmemDW6785J5gaGvvwtZXC/+RrOYzJDMGDp4JkAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAgtyOc/3FoGky/JDKBp5rDxTFPQ1TBbf0kPTELqY+zVhOvtXvwZJCTDOsdWQ05ZKwfq0qPtYSKmJE5je2nwYBBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:FXJFKYYquT8mBMevltVEZAczkbT+oJL1T6Eb6+jrkBc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNg9sGUmemDW6785J5gaGvvwtZXC/+RrOYzJDMGDp4JkAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCt0IVCsmyCiYwKtpSqrKzFl+CSI8ehtMpAKKkE/DBz4Gn6Pji9uYyEpy0p7OpWvljPna1SgtZJC2PxkRB+e3gc="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-jHj4-review-r1-hy3-primary-154-durable-fork-implementation","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:55:17.375954504Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"83be1dc0-30d2-48de-9dd6-0bd560241e3f","comment_uuid":"f747fb87-319c-424e-9f1f-6a03cda5cd92","author":"pp3g-jHj4-review-r1-hy3-primary-154-durable-fork-implementation","content":"=== RESULT PART 2/3 — 4-POST CLASSIFICATION + RETRY BUDGET ===\n--- (3) 4-POST-vs-3 on #235 row 1 — CLASSIFIED: HARNESS / TEST-ISOLATION ARTIFACT ---\nIndependent of r2 (luna, FAIL) and r4 (mimo, PASS): the 3-POST bound IS durable; the 4th POST is NOT produced by the fork's chat-completion retry budget.\nEvidence (WHY/WHAT/HOW-CERTAIN):\n1. The fork's only product-level retry of the LLM stream is Effect.retry(SessionRetry.policy(...)) at processor.ts:660-674, wrapping the ENTIRE llm.stream effect. Each retry = one new streamText POST.\n2. retry.ts stops the budget when meta.attempt > RETRY_MAX_RETRIES(2) AND isBoundedRetryCode. The #235 client WARNs PROVE meta.attempt is 1-based: logged 'retry attempt=1', 'retry attempt=2', then 'retry budget exhausted attempt=3 totalPOSTs=3'. So the fork emitted exactly 3 POSTs (initial + 2 retries). Empirical, not inferred.\n3. The MAIN chat path (prompt.ts:1272 handle.process) does NOT pass retries, so llm.ts:350 sets maxRetries: input.retries ?? 0 = 0. The AI SDK's second retry layer is DISABLED in main chat. r2's hypothesis (AI-SDK maxRetries adds a POST above the fork budget) CANNOT apply to the main chat path — there is no such layer there.\n4. provider.ts fetch wrapper has NO retry loop (only isRetryable metadata). No other product retry exists.\n5. Therefore the 4th POST must come from a request the fork's chat-completion budget does not govern. Strongest candidate: ensureTitle (prompt.ts:193-235) issues a SEPARATE llm.stream({...retries:2...}) (line 234) for a fresh session's first message — a distinct provider call counted by server.js's global postCount (increments on every req 'end', all modes). Title-gen uses maxRetries:2; a mid-stream body-idle error is NOT retried by the AI SDK, so it contributes exactly 1 POST. 1 (title) + 3 (chat fork-retry) = 4. Matches the server's 4 POSTs precisely.\nConclusion: 3-POST bound for chat completion is correct + durable. 4-POST count is a test-isolation artifact (matrix counts ALL provider POSTs, not just the chat-completion retry loop). Supports r4 (PASS); refutes r2's FAIL on this point.\n\n--- (3b) Retry-budget semantics — PASS ---\n- Error-class-scoped: RETRY_BOUNDED_CODES (retry.ts:37-42) = {ProviderResponseStreamError, ProviderHeaderTimeoutError, ECONNRESET, ZlibError}; only these capped at 2 retries; 429/5xx/usage-limit keep unbounded retry-after (intentional). OK\n- Per-attempt WARN: retry.ts:229 logs 'retry' with attempt + nextDelay (logs show 2000ms then 4000ms — matches delay() exponential backoff). OK\n- Terminal WARN: retry.ts:219 logs 'retry budget exhausted' attempt=3 totalPOSTs=3 then Cause.done. OK\n- totalPOSTs=meta.attempt(3) correct under 1-based counting (proven by client logs).","created_at":"2026-08-08T04:55:17.370127843Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:FXJFKYYquT8mBMevltVEZAczkbT+oJL1T6Eb6+jrkBc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNg9sGUmemDW6785J5gaGvvwtZXC/+RrOYzJDMGDp4JkAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA63iGTMUMJ8XLdFaaRWoSivTd29s3vrxttGqv0aTGQHHnouaMeSF2cq+7HGZOVDn9p8EYAwNufj8TkYcf/QplDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:FXJFKYYquT8mBMevltVEZAczkbT+oJL1T6Eb6+jrkBc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNg9sGUmemDW6785J5gaGvvwtZXC/+RrOYzJDMGDp4JkAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL4yqSiYSP1eBAIrqjjpPKg4tgop++d3NczvTP5H+K9UszNCb4/Bpi1N/tj/wzZTWNZKcJ4L3CTcJWtw+fheVws="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-jHj4-review-r1-hy3-primary-154-durable-fork-implementation","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:55:32.250149348Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"83be1dc0-30d2-48de-9dd6-0bd560241e3f","comment_uuid":"deaffb18-1387-4e30-972b-b5814e85596f","author":"pp3g-jHj4-review-r1-hy3-primary-154-durable-fork-implementation","content":"=== RESULT PART 3/3 — EDGE CASES + FINDINGS + VERDICT ===\n--- (4) Edge cases ---\nMUST FIX: none.\nSHOULD CONSIDER:\n- Native runtime path NOT wrapped by safeIterable. llm.ts:395 returns result.stream directly for flags.experimentalNativeLlm; llm/native-runtime.ts:103-104 builds its stream via Stream.scoped(Stream.unwrap(...)) without safeIterable. If the native iterator return() can also hang on error, the #154 deadlock class recurs there. Native is opt-in/experimental (lower risk) but the same defensive wrapper should be applied for symmetry. (llm.ts:395, llm/native-runtime.ts:103)\n- Title-generation stream uses retries:2 -> maxRetries:2 (prompt.ts:234). Under a body-idle fault it is not retried by the AI SDK (mid-stream error), so it adds 1 POST — but if a future AI-SDK version retries mid-stream errors, title-gen could emit up to 3 POSTs, inflating matrix counts. Document/isolate in harness assertions. (prompt.ts:234)\n- stream.transport.ts:1128 also calls Stream.fromAsyncIterable(events.stream) on a different (event) stream — out of #154 scope, but the same return()-hang class could apply; flag for separate review.\n\nNITS: none blocking.\n\n--- NOTABLE POSITIVES ---\n- Fix is minimal + surgical: safeIterable ~17-line pure wrapper; retry budget small, well-commented. Low blast radius.\n- Comments document effect finalizer semantics, the 1-based attempt assumption, and the #191 config-scope note — good reasoning preservation per AGENTS.md.\n- Error surfacing (ERROR + exit 1) + turn-level timeoutOrElse ('Turn stalled') together bound BOTH raw-body and parsed-stream stall classes — a complete fix, not just the interim binary patch from #145.\n\n--- WHAT-NOT-TESTED / RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY ---\n- Did not read the #235 matrix-run log (matrix-run/ artifacts outside sandbox filesystem allow-list); the 4th-POST source is inferred from source tracing + the client WARN sequence, not the server log directly. Certainty: evidence-based (high) but not 100% — exact 4th-POST identity (title-gen vs other internal call) is inferred.\n- Did not compile/run the binary; compile-readiness rests on source + the #235 gate result (65/67, row1 gate PASS).\n\n=== FINAL VERDICT: PASS ===\nThe #154 durable source fix is correct and compile-ready. safeIterable removes the silent-hang root cause; the 3-POST retry budget is durable + correctly error-class-scoped; compile-readiness markers ('Body read timed out', 'Turn stalled', ERROR, exit 1) are present in source. The row-1 4-POST-vs-3 discrepancy is a harness/test-isolation artifact (4th POST = separate title-generation request; main-chat maxRetries=0 disables any AI-SDK second retry layer), NOT a product defect. One non-blocking SHOULD-CONSIDER: extend safeIterable to the native-runtime path for symmetry.","created_at":"2026-08-08T04:55:32.243981894Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:FXJFKYYquT8mBMevltVEZAczkbT+oJL1T6Eb6+jrkBc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNg9sGUmemDW6785J5gaGvvwtZXC/+RrOYzJDMGDp4JkAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA8SIZyVLo6/+j1DUDpSJNlMbyMHGmCwS8hW37KMGehwq3wC2f9AejJ4h7NfUQs0lT6PVe8Qh/Ab55De6ai68zBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:FXJFKYYquT8mBMevltVEZAczkbT+oJL1T6Eb6+jrkBc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNg9sGUmemDW6785J5gaGvvwtZXC/+RrOYzJDMGDp4JkAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJUTtifnd0vpVqsvGaNCT0zla3n5AsdGhy21APgVJAq9iR+FH1RH36Rn7oRN+/odSixRRS3SZwVz+gQ3eMfBEg0="}
